# PN3: a bare top-level function in an app stays an error; the message
# names both choices, the program's u: and a helper's h:.
== SOURCE
h_alf := { _r / 2 }
== ERROR
error[bad-binding]: a top-level function is the program's or a helper: write u:h_alf (the program's) or h:h_alf (a helper) at 0..19
